.TH DOCUBROWSE.CONFIG 5 2026-09-13 "DocuBrowse 1.5.2" "DocuBrowse Manual"
.SH NAME
docubrowse.config \- configuration file for DocuBrowse
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/docubrowse.config
.br
.I ./docubrowse.config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docubrowse.config
configures the DocuBrowse server and command-line tools.
DocuBrowse reads the first configuration file it finds, checking the
system-wide
.I /etc/docubrowse.config
before a
.I docubrowse.config
located beside the application (or in the per-user data directory of a
packaged installation).
.P
If no file is found, built-in defaults apply, except for
.IR doc_dir ,
which has no default: until a document directory is configured, the web
interface shows a prompt and commands that need one exit with an error.
.P
Each line has the form
.IR "key = value" .
Surrounding whitespace is ignored.
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.RB \[aq] # \[aq]
are ignored.
Matching
.B DOCUBROWSE_*
environment variables override the file, and command-line options override
both.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B doc_dir
Primary directory whose documents are scanned and indexed.
No default; must be set before indexing.
Additional scan directories are managed separately and stored in
.IR scan_dirs.txt .
.TP
.B db_path
Path to the SQLite database.
Defaults to
.I du\-docs.db
beside the application.
.TP
.B port
TCP port for the HTTP server.
Defaults to
.BR 8643 .
.TP
.B work_dir
Working directory where DocuBrowse keeps its database and supporting files.
Defaults to the application directory.
.TP
.B lang
Active interface and document language.
One of
.BR en " (default),"
.BR ja ,
.BR ko ,
.BR zh ", or"
.BR zh\-hant .
A single install serves one language at a time; switching languages between
English and any CJK language requires a rescan to rebuild the index for the
new language.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The following variables override the corresponding configuration keys.
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_DOC_DIR
Overrides
.IR doc_dir .
.TP
.BR DOCUBROWSE_DB ", " DOCUBROWSE_DB_PATH
Override
.IR db_path .
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_PORT
Overrides
.IR port .
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_WORK_DIR
Overrides
.IR work_dir .
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_LANG
Overrides
.IR lang .
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Base URL of the Ollama API used for embeddings and synopses.
A bare
.I host:port
is accepted; the scheme defaults to
.IR http:// .
Also accepted as
.BR DOCUBROWSE_OLLAMA_HOST .
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_LLM_BACKEND
Text-generation backend for document synopses:
.I ollama
(default) or
.IR litellm .
The
.I litellm
backend routes through LiteLLM, reaching many providers through one
interface. Embeddings always use Ollama.
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_LLM_MODEL
Model for the
.I litellm
backend, for example
.IR anthropic/claude-opus-4-7 .
Required with that backend: the per-language defaults are Ollama tags that
LiteLLM cannot route.
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_LLM_API_BASE
Optional self-hosted LiteLLM gateway URL.
Empty means LiteLLM calls the provider directly.
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_LLM_API_KEY
Key for the
.I litellm
backend: the gateway key when
.B DOCUBROWSE_LLM_API_BASE
is set, otherwise left unset so LiteLLM reads the provider's own variable.
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_LLM_MAX_TOKENS
Optional output cap for the
.I litellm
backend, useful for hybrid reasoning models.
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_TRUSTED_CIDRS
Comma-separated CIDRs or addresses, in addition to loopback, permitted to
reach the server.
Empty means loopback only.
Ranges wider than
.I /24
(IPv4) or
.I /120
(IPv6) are refused.
This is not authentication; use it only for a private-network reverse proxy.
.TP
.B DOCUBROWSE_ALLOWED_HOSTS
Comma-separated Host header names accepted in addition to loopback.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/docubrowse.config
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I ./docubrowse.config
Per-directory configuration file.
.SH EXAMPLES
A minimal configuration:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
# docubrowse.config
doc_dir  = ~/Documents
port     = 8643
lang     = en
.EE
.in
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docubrowser (1),
.BR docuback (1)
